{"id":"mahabharata-3-272","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":272,"title":"द्विसप्तत्यधिकद्विशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 272 · Indrajit binds the brothers","summary":{"en":"Grieving for Kumbhakarna, Prahasta and Dhumraksha, Ravana sends his son Indrajit. Fighting invisibly from the sky, Indrajit covers Rama and Lakshmana with arrows until both fall to the ground.","kn":"ಕುಂಭಕರ್ಣ, ಪ್ರಹಸ್ತ, ಧೂಮ್ರಾಕ್ಷರಿಗಾಗಿ ದುಃಖಿಸುತ್ತಾ ರಾವಣನು ಮಗ ಇಂದ್ರಜಿತನನ್ನು ಕಳುಹಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಆಕಾಶದಿಂದ ಅದೃಶ್ಯನಾಗಿ ಹೋರಾಡುತ್ತಾ ಇಂದ್ರಜಿತನು ಶ್ರೀರಾಮ ಲಕ್ಷ್ಮಣರನ್ನು ಬಾಣಗಳಿಂದ ಮುಚ್ಚಿ ಇಬ್ಬರೂ ನೆಲಕ್ಕುರುಳುವಂತೆ ಮಾಡುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"कुम्भकर्ण, प्रहस्त और धूम्राक्ष के लिए शोक करता रावण अपने पुत्र इन्द्रजित को भेजता है। आकाश से अदृश्य होकर लड़ते हुए इन्द्रजित श्रीराम और लक्ष्मण को बाणों से ढक देता है, जब तक दोनों भूमि पर नहीं गिर जाते।","te":"కుంభకర్ణుడు, ప్రహస్తుడు, ధూమ్రాక్షుల కోసం దుఃఖిస్తూ రావణుడు కుమారుడు ఇంద్రజిత్తును పంపుతాడు. ఆకాశం నుండి అదృశ్యంగా పోరాడుతూ ఇంద్రజిత్తు శ్రీరామలక్ష్మణులను బాణాలతో కప్పివేసి ఇద్దరూ నేలకు ఒరిగేలా చేస్తాడు.","ta":"கும்பகர்ணன், ப்ரஹஸ்தன், தூம்ராக்ஷனுக்காக வருந்திய ராவணன் தன் மகன் இந்திரஜித்தை அனுப்புகிறான். வானிலிருந்து மறைந்து போரிடும் இந்திரஜித் ஸ்ரீராமரையும் லக்ஷ்மணனையும் அம்புகளால் மூடி இருவரும் தரையில் வீழச் செய்கிறான்.","ml":"കുംഭകർണ്ണനെയും പ്രഹസ്തനെയും ധൂമ്രാക്ഷനെയും ഓർത്ത് ദുഃഖിക്കുന്ന രാവണൻ തന്റെ പുത്രൻ ഇന്ദ്രജിത്തിനെ അയക്കുന്നു. ആകാശത്തുനിന്ന് അദൃശ്യനായി പോരാടുന്ന ഇന്ദ്രജിത്ത് രാമനെയും ലക്ഷ്മണനെയും അമ്പുകൾകൊണ്ട് മൂടി, ഇരുവരും നിലത്തുവീഴുംവരെ."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.272; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"द्रौपदीहरणपर्व","titleEn":"Draupadiharana Parva (Abduction of Draupadi)","verses":[{"text":"मार्कण्डेय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Markandeya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"ततः श्रुत्वा हतं संख्ये कुम्भकर्णं सहानुगम् ।\nप्रहस्तं च महेष्वासं धूम्राक्षं चातितेजसम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing that Kumbhakarna and his followers, Prahasta the great archer, and the very fiery Dhumraksha had been killed in battle,"}},{"n":2,"text":"पुत्रमिन्द्रजितं शूरं रावणः प्रत्यभाषत ।\nजहि रामममित्रघ्न सुग्रीवं च सलक्ष्मणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ravana spoke to his heroic son Indrajit: \"Kill Rama, destroyer of foes, and Sugriva, with Lakshmana."}},{"n":3,"text":"त्वया हि मम सत्पुत्र यशो दीप्तमुपार्जितम् ।\nजित्वा वज्रधरं संख्ये सहस्राक्षं शचीपतिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"My good son, you have won blazing fame by defeating in battle the thunderbolt-wielder, thousand-eyed Indra, husband of Shachi."}},{"n":4,"text":"अन्तर्हितः प्रकाशो वा दिव्यैर्दत्तवरैः शरैः ।\nजहि शत्रूनमित्रघ्न मम शस्त्रभृतां वर ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hidden or in the open, with arrows given you by divine boons, kill my enemies, best of those who bear arms."}},{"n":5,"text":"रामलक्ष्मणसुग्रीवाः शरस्पर्शं न तेऽनघ ।\nसमर्थाः प्रतिसंसोढुं कुतस्तदनुयायिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Rama, Lakshmana, and Sugriva cannot bear the touch of your arrows, blameless one; how then their followers?"}},{"n":6,"text":"अकृता या प्रहस्तेन कुम्भकर्णेन चानघ ।\nखरस्यापचितिः संख्ये तां गच्छस्व महाभुज ॥","meaning":{"en":"Take the revenge for Khara that Prahasta and Kumbhakarna did not accomplish in battle, mighty-armed one."}},{"n":7,"text":"त्वमद्य निशितैर्बाणैर्हत्वा शत्रून्ससैनिकान् ।\nप्रतिनन्दय मां पुत्र पुरा बद्ध्वेव वासवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Today kill the enemy and their soldiers with sharp arrows and delight me, my son, as you did when you once bound Indra.\""}},{"n":8,"text":"इत्युक्तः स तथेत्युक्त्वा रथमास्थाय दंशितः ।\nप्रययाविन्द्रजिद्राजंस्तूर्णमायोधनं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus told, Indrajit said \"So be it,\" armored himself, mounted his chariot, and, O king, quickly went to the battlefield."}},{"n":9,"text":"तत्र विश्राव्य विस्पष्टं नाम राक्षसपुंगवः ।\nआह्वयामास समरे लक्ष्मणं शुभलक्षणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There the best of rakshasas announced his name clearly and challenged the auspicious Lakshmana to battle."}},{"n":10,"text":"तं लक्ष्मणोऽप्यभ्यधावत्प्रगृह्य सशरं धनुः ।\nत्रासयंस्तलघोषेण सिंहः क्षुद्रमृगं यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lakshmana, taking up his bow and arrow, ran at him, terrifying him with the twang of his bowstring, as a lion terrifies a small beast."}},{"n":11,"text":"तयोः समभवद्युद्धं सुमहज्जयगृद्धिनोः ।\nदिव्यास्त्रविदुषोस्तीव्रमन्योन्यस्पर्धिनोस्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"A great fight began between those two, eager for victory, knowers of divine weapons, fiercely vying with each other."}},{"n":12,"text":"रावणिस्तु यदा नैनं विशेषयति सायकैः ।\nततो गुरुतरं यत्नमातिष्ठद्बलिनां वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When Ravana's son could not get the better of Lakshmana with arrows, that best of the strong made a still greater effort."}},{"n":13,"text":"तत एनं महावेगैरर्दयामास तोमरैः ।\nतानागतान्स चिच्छेद सौमित्रिर्निशितैः शरैः ।\nते निकृत्ताः शरैस्तीक्ष्णैर्न्यपतन्वसुधातले ॥","meaning":{"en":"He then harassed Lakshmana with very swift spears, but the son of Sumitra cut them down as they came with sharp arrows, and they fell to the ground."}},{"n":14,"text":"तमङ्गदो वालिसुतः श्रीमानुद्यम्य पादपम् ।\nअभिद्रुत्य महावेगस्ताडयामास मूर्धनि ॥","meaning":{"en":"The splendid Angada, Vali's son, lifted a tree and rushed at Indrajit and struck him on the head."}},{"n":15,"text":"तस्येन्द्रजिदसंभ्रान्तः प्रासेनोरसि वीर्यवान् ।\nप्रहर्तुमैच्छत्तं चास्य प्रासं चिच्छेद लक्ष्मणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The valiant Indrajit, unshaken, wanted to strike Angada in the chest with a lance, but Lakshmana cut the lance in two."}},{"n":16,"text":"तमभ्याशगतं वीरमङ्गदं रावणात्मजः ।\nगदयाताडयत्सव्ये पार्श्वे वानरपुंगवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the hero Angada came near, Ravana's son struck that bull among monkeys with a mace on the left side."}},{"n":17,"text":"तमचिन्त्य प्रहारं स बलवान्वालिनः सुतः ।\nससर्जेन्द्रजितः क्रोधाच्छालस्कन्धममित्रजित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Strong Angada, son of Vali, paid no heed to the blow and, in anger, hurled the trunk of a sala tree at Indrajit."}},{"n":18,"text":"सोऽङ्गदेन रुषोत्सृष्टो वधायेन्द्रजितस्तरुः ।\nजघानेन्द्रजितः पार्थ रथं साश्वं ससारथिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hurled in anger by Angada to kill Indrajit, the tree struck Indrajit's chariot with its horses and charioteer, son of Pritha."}},{"n":19,"text":"ततो हताश्वात्प्रस्कन्द्य रथात्स हतसारथिः ।\nतत्रैवान्तर्दधे राजन्मायया रावणात्मजः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, with his horses and charioteer killed, Ravana's son leapt from the chariot and, O king, vanished on the spot by his magic."}},{"n":20,"text":"अन्तर्हितं विदित्वा तं बहुमायं च राक्षसम् ।\nरामस्तं देशमागम्य तत्सैन्यं पर्यरक्षत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Knowing that the rakshasa, a master of many illusions, had disappeared, Rama came to that spot and guarded the army."}},{"n":21,"text":"स राममुद्दिश्य शरैस्ततो दत्तवरैस्तदा ।\nविव्याध सर्वगात्रेषु लक्ष्मणं च महारथम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Aiming at Rama, Indrajit then pierced all his limbs with arrows given by boons, and also the great chariot-fighter Lakshmana."}},{"n":22,"text":"तमदृश्यं शरैः शूरौ माययान्तर्हितं तदा ।\nयोधयामासतुरुभौ रावणिं रामलक्ष्मणौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Though Indrajit was hidden by illusion, the two heroes fought the son of Ravana with arrows."}},{"n":23,"text":"स रुषा सर्वगात्रेषु तयोः पुरुषसिंहयोः ।\nव्यसृजत्सायकान्भूयः शतशोऽथ सहस्रशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Furious, he again shot hundreds and thousands of arrows into every limb of those two lions among men."}},{"n":24,"text":"तमदृश्यं विचिन्वन्तः सृजन्तमनिशं शरान् ।\nहरयो विविशुर्व्योम प्रगृह्य महतीः शिलाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Searching for the unseen one, who kept pouring arrows, the monkeys leapt into the sky with huge rocks."}},{"n":25,"text":"तांश्च तौ चाप्यदृश्यः स शरैर्विव्याध राक्षसः ।\nस भृशं ताडयन्वीरो रावणिर्माययावृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The invisible rakshasa pierced them and the two brothers with his arrows, and Ravana's son, shrouded in illusion, struck hard."}},{"n":26,"text":"तौ शरैराचितौ वीरौ भ्रातरौ रामलक्ष्मणौ ।\nपेततुर्गगनाद्भूमिं सूर्याचन्द्रमसाविव ॥","meaning":{"en":"The two heroic brothers, Rama and Lakshmana, studded with arrows, fell from the sky to the ground like the sun and moon."}}]}]}